new file mode 100644
index 0000000..08024c1
--- /dev/null
+++ b/SUMMARY.md
@@ -0,0 +1,15 @@
+# Summary
+
+## Changed
+- `stockreport/report.py`: `render()` now supports `fmt="markdown"`. It uses the vendored `tabulate` with `style="pipe"` and `number_format=".2f"`. The columns and sort order are the same as the text report. The table is followed by a blank line and `**Total stock value:** <value>`.
+- `stockreport/__main__.py`: `--format` now accepts `markdown` as well as `text`.
+- `README.md`: documents the new option.
+- No tests were edited. The existing tests in `tests/test_report.py` already cover this feature.
+- Nothing under `vendor/` was touched, and no dependencies were added.
+
+## Verified
+- `python -W error::DeprecationWarning -m unittest -v` ran 3 tests, all OK. These were `test_text_output`, `test_markdown_output` and `test_cli_markdown`. Running with `-W error::DeprecationWarning` confirms no ignored legacy tabulate keywords are used.
+- `python -m stockreport inventory.csv --format markdown` printed the expected table, and the total was 461.93.
+
+## Not verified
+- I only tested with the three-row `inventory.csv`. I did not test edge cases such as an empty inventory or names containing `|`. The vendored `tabulate` does not escape pipes, so such names would break the markdown table.
